 "name": "Scenic Beauty of Soil and Water Conservation Works (SBE)",
 "description": "Faithful replication of Peng & Han (2018), Water 10:407. Participants first see 16 photographs of soil and water conservation structures in Taiwan (check dams, ground sills, revetments, detention ponds and a grassed waterway) as a 3-second quick look, then rate each picture one at a time from 0 (extremely dislike) to 9 (extremely like) for scenic beauty, plus five further questions: integration of the structure with nature, the waterscape, visual richness, the shape of the structure and perceived safety. Analysis: Scenic Beauty Estimation (Daniel & Boster 1976): z-scores per rater, mean z per picture minus the mean of all 16 pictures, times 100; compare structure types. Each trial records the structure type and the picture's SBE rank in the paper.\n\nPictures: the 16 photographs printed in the paper's Table 4 (CC BY 4.0, taken by the authors), used with credit; the template is removed if the authors object.\n\nDifferences from the original study: (1) online and self-paced instead of slides projected in a classroom for 16 s each; pictures appear in random order; (2) the paper gives only the 0–9 scale and anchors for question 1; questions 2–6 use the same 0–9 scale with anchors written for this template, and all question wordings are paraphrased from the paper's descriptions; (3) the paper lists the basic data (gender, age, occupation, studied lessons, understanding of the structures' function) but not the answer options; the options here are our own; (4) pictures are the small versions printed in the paper (about 274 × 206 px).",
